(6111484, 899766, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives:I''m a sucker for unusual POVs and this one qualifies! There are quite a lot of leading lines in this image which draw our eye along up past the paper to the dual door handles - I like how that happens. The whole environment is quite intriguing, the reflected light looks like it comes from a window making this an internal corridor. The handles themselves are interesting - a hotel? An apartment block? I''m not sure.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not too much - inherent interest is low but the scene is the scene.<br/> <br/>Overall: Quite an interesting shot but I think scenes with quite low inherent interest need a bit more story to them than this offers up.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives:I''m a sucker for unusual POVs and this one qualifies! There are quite a lot of leading lines in this image which draw our eye along up past the paper to the dual door handles - I like how that happens. The whole environment is quite intriguing, the reflected light looks like it comes from a window making this an internal corridor. The handles themselves are interesting - a hotel? An apartment block? I''m not sure. Critical stuff: Not too much - inherent interest is low but the scene is the scene. Overall: Quite an interesting shot but I think scenes with quite low inherent interest need a bit more story to them than this offers up.', '2010-08-01 11:03:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6111493, 900481, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: The colours here are quite nice; particularly the pinkish cluster, I''m also a fan of the near black sky too - that slight residual daylight blue is compelling.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Although I''m a fan of the use of blur, I just don''t think this image hangs together. I like the idea, but it just doesn''t feel crafted. I think a squarer crop may have appealed more - the top 1/4 of the image doesn''t contribute much.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like the idea behind the shot but it lacks some magic for me.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: The colours here are quite nice; particularly the pinkish cluster, I''m also a fan of the near black sky too - that slight residual daylight blue is compelling. Critical stuff: Although I''m a fan of the use of blur, I just don''t think this image hangs together. I like the idea, but it just doesn''t feel crafted. I think a squarer crop may have appealed more - the top 1/4 of the image doesn''t contribute much. Overall: I like the idea behind the shot but it lacks some magic for me.', '2010-08-01 11:14:18.000000', NULL, 1),
