(6121445, 900627, 20130, '<td valign="top">well thats a different flower shot!</td>', 'well thats a different flower shot!', '2010-08-07 04:17:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121446, 900850, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Very effectively done, the bold framing offer by the architecture, the dividing line between your air and water elelements, the subtle reflection - all good stuff. Of course the fish is the star.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Should the fish (singlular) be the star? Or should the fish (pleural) be the stars. I ''m not sure.... I feel a little cheated - perhaps this one was a different colour, but the overall effect is one of it escaping selctiving coloring / desaturation.<br/> <br/>Overall: I do like this, but not quite as much as I would like to have.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Very effectively done, the bold framing offer by the architecture, the dividing line between your air and water elelements, the subtle reflection - all good stuff. Of course the fish is the star. Critical stuff: Should the fish (singlular) be the star? Or should the fish (pleural) be the stars. I ''m not sure.... I feel a little cheated - perhaps this one was a different colour, but the overall effect is one of it escaping selctiving coloring / desaturation. Overall: I do like this, but not quite as much as I would like to have.', '2010-08-07 04:24:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121450, 900443, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like that this is here in the Free Study offering - it stands out from the crowd. Coloring is fairly gorgeous and the lighting is perfect for the scene. The compositional elements are of course eclectic. I also like the way the texture of the individual pieces are apparent.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The image is perhaps over-contrived; not really a problem in itself, whenever we point a camera at something and choose our framing we create something that is contrived. Here though, it seems a little forced... Almost cynical, and of course the title doesn''t help. It hasn''t escaped me it could just be an ironic image and by me even attempting to construct a comment like this for a bunch of stuff in a basement I fall into the trap.<br/> <br/>Overall: Whatever your intention with this image, it has engaged me, it has made me question what we / I value in an image, surely forcing that reflection upon a viewer constitutes art. Here, viewing has become dialogue - and that dialogue (if not the image) was emergent and natural, not contrived.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like that this is here in the Free Study offering - it stands out from the crowd. Coloring is fairly gorgeous and the lighting is perfect for the scene. The compositional elements are of course eclectic. I also like the way the texture of the individual pieces are apparent. Critical stuff: The image is perhaps over-contrived; not really a problem in itself, whenever we point a camera at something and choose our framing we create something that is contrived. Here though, it seems a little forced... Almost cynical, and of course the title doesn''t help. It hasn''t escaped me it could just be an ironic image and by me even attempting to construct a comment like this for a bunch of stuff in a basement I fall into the trap. Overall: Whatever your intention with this image, it has engaged me, it has made me question what we / I value in an image, surely forcing that reflection upon a viewer constitutes art. Here, viewing has become dialogue - and that dialogue (if not the image) was emergent and natural, not contrived.', '2010-08-07 04:43:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121451, 900453, 100393, '<td valign="top">Subtle tones and the leading lines make this a standout landscape.</td>', 'Subtle tones and the leading lines make this a standout landscape.', '2010-08-07 04:45:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121456, 900825, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I am a fan of Lensbaby images, so you have a headstart - additionally, I like the subject matter and the high contrast, I''m glad you''ve let the highlights blow.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: More here than I''d like to put down, but here goes.... Although the selective focus is in the right place, it is missed slightly - I wonder what aperture ring you used... I know how tricky the LB can be to use. I do respect your use of colour here and in a way it does bring something unique to the image but my poor conditioned brain yearns for this to be in monochrome, with a vignette... Does that make me complicit in the propagation of a cliched image.... Probably.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like your overall vision here, but I perhaps need to evolve my own tastes before I can fully appreciate it''s merits.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I am a fan of Lensbaby images, so you have a headstart - additionally, I like the subject matter and the high contrast, I''m glad you''ve let the highlights blow. Critical stuff: More here than I''d like to put down, but here goes.... Although the selective focus is in the right place, it is missed slightly - I wonder what aperture ring you used... I know how tricky the LB can be to use. I do respect your use of colour here and in a way it does bring something unique to the image but my poor conditioned brain yearns for this to be in monochrome, with a vignette... Does that make me complicit in the propagation of a cliched image.... Probably. Overall: I like your overall vision here, but I perhaps need to evolve my own tastes before I can fully appreciate it''s merits.', '2010-08-07 04:53:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121462, 900740, 100393, '<td valign="top">Unusually well balanced in so many ways.</td>', 'Unusually well balanced in so many ways.', '2010-08-07 04:57:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121471, 900658, 100393, '<td valign="top">Startling high macro image. Lovely coloration too. I don''t get nearly this quality with my macro images. I''m wondering if this is Jason''s entry.</td>', 'Startling high macro image. Lovely coloration too. I don''t get nearly this quality with my macro images. I''m wondering if this is Jason''s entry.', '2010-08-07 05:03:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121487, 900970, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: bold abstract with really nice colours - always good to see people taking a chance in the Fre Study. I like that I can still see this is a vase of flowers.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I like the image, but I think it is suboptimal, the colour are great but the junction between them jars a little. I think adding some diffusion in your workflow would have worked wonders to mellow the image a little.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very nearly there, but falls just a little short of my sweet spot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: bold abstract with really nice colours - always good to see people taking a chance in the Fre Study. I like that I can still see this is a vase of flowers. Critical stuff: I like the image, but I think it is suboptimal, the colour are great but the junction between them jars a little. I think adding some diffusion in your workflow would have worked wonders to mellow the image a little. Overall: Very nearly there, but falls just a little short of my sweet spot.', '2010-08-07 05:12:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121508, 899671, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: The POV and leading lines are excellent compositional elements. I like the colours too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The guy in the background looks like he''s singing a camp musical number - that kind of clashes with the rest of the image. I just can''t take it seriously - sorry.<br/> <br/>Overall: I think I see what you were going for, but given the reference in your title, you miss the required mood by a mile. I am sorry to be harsh though. I promise that I tried to like it.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: The POV and leading lines are excellent compositional elements. I like the colours too. Critical stuff: The guy in the background looks like he''s singing a camp musical number - that kind of clashes with the rest of the image. I just can''t take it seriously - sorry. Overall: I think I see what you were going for, but given the reference in your title, you miss the required mood by a mile. I am sorry to be harsh though. I promise that I tried to like it.', '2010-08-07 05:29:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121512, 899747, 63812, '<td valign="top">a winner for me..10 (first one after 297 votes)</td>', 'a winner for me..10 (first one after 297 votes)', '2010-08-07 05:32:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121518, 900867, 63812, '<td valign="top">very good</td>', 'very good', '2010-08-07 05:36:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121522, 900892, 63812, '<td valign="top">love this..nice composition and colors 9</td>', 'love this..nice composition and colors 9', '2010-08-07 05:39:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121524, 898378, 63812, '<td valign="top">excellent!</td>', 'excellent!', '2010-08-07 05:41:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121526, 897792, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: The middle section of this image is startlingly good - excellent composition and truly wonderful lighting, accentuated as it is by the spray. The pose of the swimmer is excellent - the level ''gaze'' is wonderful.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The sprayers around the edge and the title. Although, of course, I see the humour in this image - it is soooo very good that I feel it shouldn''t be spoilt. I shudder to think how good your work must be to be able to ''throw'' this image out there with such a carefree attitude.<br/> <br/>Overall; Of course this is marvellously well done and your choices are your choices - they aren''t the ones I''d have made, but this is your image and given your vision, I''m not sure how it could be much better. I consider it a little spoilt but I''m giving it a 10 nonetheless.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: The middle section of this image is startlingly good - excellent composition and truly wonderful lighting, accentuated as it is by the spray. The pose of the swimmer is excellent - the level ''gaze'' is wonderful. Critical stuff: The sprayers around the edge and the title. Although, of course, I see the humour in this image - it is soooo very good that I feel it shouldn''t be spoilt. I shudder to think how good your work must be to be able to ''throw'' this image out there with such a carefree attitude. Overall; Of course this is marvellously well done and your choices are your choices - they aren''t the ones I''d have made, but this is your image and given your vision, I''m not sure how it could be much better. I consider it a little spoilt but I''m giving it a 10 nonetheless.', '2010-08-07 05:46:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121527, 899823, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Perfect use of quite subtle tone-mapping; this is great quirky stuff. The dog, the toys, the car - all these elements make for a highly interesting scene. But more than that, you have the measure of it - you''re processing resonates with the image to produce something that just works.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all<br/> <br/>Overall: Excellent, well executed interesting image.<br/> <br/>I keep coming back to this. I like its funky feel. Bumping from 9 to 10.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Perfect use of quite subtle tone-mapping; this is great quirky stuff. The dog, the toys, the car - all these elements make for a highly interesting scene. But more than that, you have the measure of it - you''re processing resonates with the image to produce something that just works. Critical stuff: Nothing at all Overall: Excellent, well executed interesting image. I keep coming back to this. I like its funky feel. Bumping from 9 to 10.', '2010-08-07 05:48:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121529, 900135, 28710, '<td valign="top">nice shot, with good lighting, could use a bit of work in processing by lightening the woman''s face, and possibly the horse''s just a hair as well as toning down the sharpening just a bit IMHO. There are a few distracting flecks that distract as well.</td>', 'nice shot, with good lighting, could use a bit of work in processing by lightening the woman''s face, and possibly the horse''s just a hair as well as toning down the sharpening just a bit IMHO. There are a few distracting flecks that distract as well.', '2010-08-07 06:11:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121532, 900442, 28710, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. I like how the two flowers in the foreground complement the color of the mountains, although they do feel like they ''missed'' a tiny bit.<br/> <br/>It looks like you used HDR here (note the characteristic haloing around the edges of the mountains), so I''m a bit curious as to why there is so much detail lost in the shadows, especially with the house.<br/> <br/>Nice pic anyhow.</td>', 'Beautiful. I like how the two flowers in the foreground complement the color of the mountains, although they do feel like they ''missed'' a tiny bit. It looks like you used HDR here (note the characteristic haloing around the edges of the mountains), so I''m a bit curious as to why there is so much detail lost in the shadows, especially with the house. Nice pic anyhow.', '2010-08-07 06:14:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121535, 900484, 28710, '<td valign="top">Unusual, it''s like a Triangle of HDR processing with high tonal range and haloing and the rest with regular processing. <br/> <br/>Odd choice. Also, the colors seem a bit ''all over the place. I like the soft tan in the sand and the soft green in the water, but the sky kind of detracts from that.<br/> <br/>I don''t dislike it though</td>', 'Unusual, it''s like a Triangle of HDR processing with high tonal range and haloing and the rest with regular processing.  Odd choice. Also, the colors seem a bit ''all over the place. I like the soft tan in the sand and the soft green in the water, but the sky kind of detracts from that. I don''t dislike it though', '2010-08-07 06:17:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121537, 900948, 28710, '<td valign="top">Great moment captured well!<br/> <br/>I find the pic a bit soft though, kind of like a missed focus or maybe not using a tripod for a long shot?</td>', 'Great moment captured well! I find the pic a bit soft though, kind of like a missed focus or maybe not using a tripod for a long shot?', '2010-08-07 06:18:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121540, 900556, 28710, '<td valign="top">This is really cool - mostly because I can''t tell what you used for a light...<br/> <br/>I like the moonlight that feels like sunlight coming through the leaves and I like the blues with the yellows of the foreground. <br/> <br/>I also like the feeling that there are faces, especially the oval on the right and above the middle rock.<br/> <br/>Very fun to look at. 8</td>', 'This is really cool - mostly because I can''t tell what you used for a light... I like the moonlight that feels like sunlight coming through the leaves and I like the blues with the yellows of the foreground.  I also like the feeling that there are faces, especially the oval on the right and above the middle rock. Very fun to look at. 8', '2010-08-07 06:20:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121541, 900867, 28710, '<td valign="top">Very, very effective use of reduced sat. An attractive pic with a strong Euro feel.</td>', 'Very, very effective use of reduced sat. An attractive pic with a strong Euro feel.', '2010-08-07 06:21:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121542, 900765, 28710, '<td valign="top">Well this one has some serious impact. Honestly, I think that it comes from the unusual blue-green that is so prominent. There''s a strong sense of nostalgia that jumps out here.<br/> <br/>The composition is fantastic and in general, I''d say that every aspect of this pic is well managed with obvious intent. Excellent!</td>', 'Well this one has some serious impact. Honestly, I think that it comes from the unusual blue-green that is so prominent. There''s a strong sense of nostalgia that jumps out here. The composition is fantastic and in general, I''d say that every aspect of this pic is well managed with obvious intent. Excellent!', '2010-08-07 06:24:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121543, 899290, 28710, '<td valign="top">Nice that you actually got the third rainbow there too on the inside. I''ve never seen a rainbow quite so strong, so it does feel a bit overdone, but it''s a heck of a job!</td>', 'Nice that you actually got the third rainbow there too on the inside. I''ve never seen a rainbow quite so strong, so it does feel a bit overdone, but it''s a heck of a job!', '2010-08-07 06:25:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121544, 900299, 28710, '<td valign="top">Very nice use of color. The red has an Asian feel and contributes well to the color of the bamboo. The smoothness of the bamboo is also well treated.<br/> <br/>Good one!</td>', 'Very nice use of color. The red has an Asian feel and contributes well to the color of the bamboo. The smoothness of the bamboo is also well treated. Good one!', '2010-08-07 06:28:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121548, 898538, 28710, '<td valign="top">What a happy little image. Great job with just the one smiling out at us and a dreamy soft look on the others. Excellent.</td>', 'What a happy little image. Great job with just the one smiling out at us and a dreamy soft look on the others. Excellent.', '2010-08-07 06:44:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121549, 900107, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Made me say ''ooooh'' when it opened. Lovely everything really, simple composition with just the right post-processing to make the most of what is here. I like how my eye is drawn to the wine glass and how that accent imbues the whole image with a sense of relaxation. The coloration reinforces the calming effect of the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: should be used as a tool for anger management so soothing is its effect.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Made me say ''ooooh'' when it opened. Lovely everything really, simple composition with just the right post-processing to make the most of what is here. I like how my eye is drawn to the wine glass and how that accent imbues the whole image with a sense of relaxation. The coloration reinforces the calming effect of the image. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: should be used as a tool for anger management so soothing is its effect.', '2010-08-07 06:45:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121550, 900682, 28710, '<td valign="top">Image feels crowded by the thickness of the border. If the border were toned back to about the same weight as at the waterline of the boat, I''d like it more.<br/> <br/>Nice work on the processing and the light beams.</td>', 'Image feels crowded by the thickness of the border. If the border were toned back to about the same weight as at the waterline of the boat, I''d like it more. Nice work on the processing and the light beams.', '2010-08-07 06:46:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121551, 896739, 28710, '<td valign="top">Perfect pose for his frame. Well spotted and very nicely processed. It feels very natural and very dreamy at the same time. 10</td>', 'Perfect pose for his frame. Well spotted and very nicely processed. It feels very natural and very dreamy at the same time. 10', '2010-08-07 06:49:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121552, 900453, 28710, '<td valign="top">A small niggle. looks like your ND filter slopped onto the lighthouse. Something slightly uneven about the lightness of it.<br/> <br/>Otherwise, very very good.</td>', 'A small niggle. looks like your ND filter slopped onto the lighthouse. Something slightly uneven about the lightness of it. Otherwise, very very good.', '2010-08-07 06:52:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121555, 900576, 120067, '<td valign="top">Interesting photo!  Love the setting!</td>', 'Interesting photo!  Love the setting!', '2010-08-07 07:10:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121566, 898690, 94241, '<td valign="top">I really like the patch of red offsetting her lips.  I really like the yin/yang thing between her hair and the background.  I recognize it as perfect textbook butterfly lighting.  Compositionally I really dig this shot.  But I''m bugged a little by the model, I feel she looks sort of dear-in-the-headlights stunned.<br/> <br/>I think it''s just she needs a different facial expression.  But I also keep wondering if there were a little more directionality to the light if it would soften her severity a little bit.</td>', 'I really like the patch of red offsetting her lips.  I really like the yin/yang thing between her hair and the background.  I recognize it as perfect textbook butterfly lighting.  Compositionally I really dig this shot.  But I''m bugged a little by the model, I feel she looks sort of dear-in-the-headlights stunned. I think it''s just she needs a different facial expression.  But I also keep wondering if there were a little more directionality to the light if it would soften her severity a little bit.', '2010-08-07 07:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121568, 900004, 12674, '<td valign="top">Nice weathery shot, and I like the Michael Scott-like title.</td>', 'Nice weathery shot, and I like the Michael Scott-like title.', '2010-08-07 07:46:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121569, 897819, 94241, '<td valign="top">I feel confused by this shot.  I''m not really sure if it''s a shot of a sunset or a minimalist silhouette or both.  Maybe it''s because the shape is a little complex.  If it were a simpler silhouette shape maybe?</td>', 'I feel confused by this shot.  I''m not really sure if it''s a shot of a sunset or a minimalist silhouette or both.  Maybe it''s because the shape is a little complex.  If it were a simpler silhouette shape maybe?', '2010-08-07 07:52:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121571, 899302, 94241, '<td valign="top">So I too like to style pictures into wild colors now and then.  But I''ve noticed that my really trippy stuff never seems to appeal to a lot of people.  I also notice most other people''s really trippy stuff doesn''t often appeal to me.  Since you do this stuff too (and I do admire the technical excellence) I wondered if you found similar response?  Hit me up a message sometime after voting''s done and let me know, would you?  :)</td>', 'So I too like to style pictures into wild colors now and then.  But I''ve noticed that my really trippy stuff never seems to appeal to a lot of people.  I also notice most other people''s really trippy stuff doesn''t often appeal to me.  Since you do this stuff too (and I do admire the technical excellence) I wondered if you found similar response?  Hit me up a message sometime after voting''s done and let me know, would you?  :)', '2010-08-07 07:57:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121572, 900827, 94241, '<td valign="top">Beautiful flower, beautiful light, beautiful chiaroscuro.  The jewelry is beautiful too, just I''m not quite sure from this viewpoint if it''s a ring or something else.</td>', 'Beautiful flower, beautiful light, beautiful chiaroscuro.  The jewelry is beautiful too, just I''m not quite sure from this viewpoint if it''s a ring or something else.', '2010-08-07 08:02:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121577, 900341, 94241, '<td valign="top">An absolutely beautiful moment.  :)<br/> <br/> <br/>I think this photo could be raised a level by some different approach in post processing.<br/> <br/>Hmm...<br/> <br/>Okay, were it up to me, here''s what I''d do.<br/> <br/>The first thing is the crop.  I think that a much tighter crop would be good in a number of ways.  Like, try cropping it down to just his head and a little bit of the water ripple.  (1) it''d bring an emotional intimacy to this.  (2) the grass in front is a bit of a barrier between viewer and subject, and I think removing most of that would be good.  (3) the bright white splotch on the right drags the eye away from the model, cutting that out would also be good.<br/> <br/>There''s also a bit of a cyan color cast to this image that I think it might look livelier if that were taken out.<br/> <br/>And finally, I''d probably try to darken the vegetation a bit.  Right now your model looks shadowed and overwhelmed by the brightness of the world.<br/> <br/>Again, beautiful shot.  :)</td>', 'An absolutely beautiful moment.  :)  I think this photo could be raised a level by some different approach in post processing. Hmm... Okay, were it up to me, here''s what I''d do. The first thing is the crop.  I think that a much tighter crop would be good in a number of ways.  Like, try cropping it down to just his head and a little bit of the water ripple.  (1) it''d bring an emotional intimacy to this.  (2) the grass in front is a bit of a barrier between viewer and subject, and I think removing most of that would be good.  (3) the bright white splotch on the right drags the eye away from the model, cutting that out would also be good. There''s also a bit of a cyan color cast to this image that I think it might look livelier if that were taken out. And finally, I''d probably try to darken the vegetation a bit.  Right now your model looks shadowed and overwhelmed by the brightness of the world. Again, beautiful shot.  :)', '2010-08-07 08:35:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121578, 900877, 94241, '<td valign="top">I understand how beautiful the edge of the building is, but the big bright white sky just dominates the composition of this image.  What if the sky had been cropped out?  A square aspect ratio might work fine for this image.  Then with the sky gone, lower the brightness slider a few notches?</td>', 'I understand how beautiful the edge of the building is, but the big bright white sky just dominates the composition of this image.  What if the sky had been cropped out?  A square aspect ratio might work fine for this image.  Then with the sky gone, lower the brightness slider a few notches?', '2010-08-07 08:41:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121579, 900931, 94241, '<td valign="top">I see the potential, but I think the image just loses too much detail in highlights and shadows.<br/> <br/>I live in a forest just like this.  You may be one of my locals for all I know.  :)   I kept getting frustrated because I could never make a photo that caught the magic of the little dappled-sunlight spots I found in the woods.  Then someone pointed out to me that sunny spots are full, bright, direct sunlight.  So, like, f/22 or so.  The shadow spots don''t get a lot of ambient light because the forest is generally kind of dark.  So, like, f/4 or so.  There''s just no earthly way for a single exposure to make dappled sunlight look good.  With that thought in mind, I started working HDR techniques for a while, and eventually it added tons to my forest shots.<br/> <br/>I highly recommend HDR for shots like this.</td>', 'I see the potential, but I think the image just loses too much detail in highlights and shadows. I live in a forest just like this.  You may be one of my locals for all I know.  :)   I kept getting frustrated because I could never make a photo that caught the magic of the little dappled-sunlight spots I found in the woods.  Then someone pointed out to me that sunny spots are full, bright, direct sunlight.  So, like, f/22 or so.  The shadow spots don''t get a lot of ambient light because the forest is generally kind of dark.  So, like, f/4 or so.  There''s just no earthly way for a single exposure to make dappled sunlight look good.  With that thought in mind, I started working HDR techniques for a while, and eventually it added tons to my forest shots. I highly recommend HDR for shots like this.', '2010-08-07 08:53:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121589, 897804, 94241, '<td valign="top">Very painterly.  I love it.</td>', 'Very painterly.  I love it.', '2010-08-07 09:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121590, 896276, 94241, '<td valign="top">Beautiful color palette.  There''s a lot of depth and dimension to this image as well.  :)</td>', 'Beautiful color palette.  There''s a lot of depth and dimension to this image as well.  :)', '2010-08-07 09:07:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121653, 900497, 65234, '<td valign="top">Beautiful detail; very three-dimensional.</td>', 'Beautiful detail; very three-dimensional.', '2010-08-07 10:58:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121659, 900914, 65234, '<td valign="top">Very regal-looking in that patch of light.</td>', 'Very regal-looking in that patch of light.', '2010-08-07 11:01:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121664, 900616, 65234, '<td valign="top">Looking appropriately wary and alert.  I like the negative space; it invites me to imagine what he''s looking at so intently.</td>', 'Looking appropriately wary and alert.  I like the negative space; it invites me to imagine what he''s looking at so intently.', '2010-08-07 11:06:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121665, 900892, 65234, '<td valign="top">A weird bug; my favorite kind :-)  I like that bright little eye and the bug''s placement in the frame.</td>', 'A weird bug; my favorite kind :-)  I like that bright little eye and the bug''s placement in the frame.', '2010-08-07 11:07:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121669, 900974, 65234, '<td valign="top">Lovely blue eyes which are nicely set off by the umbrella.  I think I would have cropped tighter to emphasize that and get rid of the multi-colored towel.  Alternatively (if I wanted to keep the cute sunglasses) I''d color the towel blue to make it less attention-grabbing.</td>', 'Lovely blue eyes which are nicely set off by the umbrella.  I think I would have cropped tighter to emphasize that and get rid of the multi-colored towel.  Alternatively (if I wanted to keep the cute sunglasses) I''d color the towel blue to make it less attention-grabbing.', '2010-08-07 11:15:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121671, 899516, 65234, '<td valign="top">Rejected one kid already, huh?  Great find.</td>', 'Rejected one kid already, huh?  Great find.', '2010-08-07 11:16:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121674, 898090, 65234, '<td valign="top">Cute story told here.</td>', 'Cute story told here.', '2010-08-07 11:17:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121678, 897977, 65234, '<td valign="top">That looks like someplace I''d really like to sit and drink in the beauty.</td>', 'That looks like someplace I''d really like to sit and drink in the beauty.', '2010-08-07 11:19:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121679, 900611, 65234, '<td valign="top">Love all the curves; looks like a fascinating place to explore.</td>', 'Love all the curves; looks like a fascinating place to explore.', '2010-08-07 11:21:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121683, 900886, 65234, '<td valign="top">Very nice tones here, and an interesting pose.  Horizon looks tilted to me, but not very purposefully.</td>', 'Very nice tones here, and an interesting pose.  Horizon looks tilted to me, but not very purposefully.', '2010-08-07 11:24:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121684, 899262, 65234, '<td valign="top">Cool abstract!</td>', 'Cool abstract!', '2010-08-07 11:24:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121686, 898163, 65234, '<td valign="top">Different perspective makes this more interesting to me than a lot of raptor headshots.  I particularly like the sweep of the neck feathers.  Nit:  I tihnk I''d fix the green reflection on the underside of his jaw and top of his neck.</td>', 'Different perspective makes this more interesting to me than a lot of raptor headshots.  I particularly like the sweep of the neck feathers.  Nit:  I tihnk I''d fix the green reflection on the underside of his jaw and top of his neck.', '2010-08-07 11:28:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121687, 900679, 65234, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.</td>', 'Nicely done.', '2010-08-07 11:29:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121689, 900453, 65234, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and detail here.</td>', 'Nice composition and detail here.', '2010-08-07 11:30:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121690, 900520, 65234, '<td valign="top">Dizzying!  Very cool image.</td>', 'Dizzying!  Very cool image.', '2010-08-07 11:30:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121691, 900656, 65234, '<td valign="top">Spiders have way too many eyeballs!  Nicely captured.</td>', 'Spiders have way too many eyeballs!  Nicely captured.', '2010-08-07 11:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121692, 899213, 65234, '<td valign="top">Nice detail.</td>', 'Nice detail.', '2010-08-07 11:32:50.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6121762, 899698, 76335, '<td valign="top">Interesting study in color and texture and light.</td>', 'Interesting study in color and texture and light.', '2010-08-07 12:40:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121764, 897388, 76335, '<td valign="top">I like it but have to say that the top quarter or so of the frame -- the negative space -- doesn''t really add anything. Cropped between the hand and the buckle, I fine the composition more effective, more direct. <br/> <br/>Still, very good.</td>', 'I like it but have to say that the top quarter or so of the frame -- the negative space -- doesn''t really add anything. Cropped between the hand and the buckle, I fine the composition more effective, more direct.  Still, very good.', '2010-08-07 12:42:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121765, 900494, 76335, '<td valign="top">Beautiful tones here. Very quiet, peaceful...</td>', 'Beautiful tones here. Very quiet, peaceful...', '2010-08-07 12:42:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121766, 898276, 76335, '<td valign="top">So glad you didn''t clone the brown spots out. I like photographs that are real. <br/> <br/>Very beautiful in spite of (and beacuase of!) nature''s little imperfections.</td>', 'So glad you didn''t clone the brown spots out. I like photographs that are real.  Very beautiful in spite of (and beacuase of!) nature''s little imperfections.', '2010-08-07 12:43:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121767, 897766, 76335, '<td valign="top">A fun summertime shot. Feels a bit soft though. You have lots of light, so you could have chosen a faster shutter speed and/or more DOF (stopped down).</td>', 'A fun summertime shot. Feels a bit soft though. You have lots of light, so you could have chosen a faster shutter speed and/or more DOF (stopped down).', '2010-08-07 12:45:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121769, 900785, 76335, '<td valign="top">Good use of negative space here.</td>', 'Good use of negative space here.', '2010-08-07 12:46:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121772, 900704, 76335, '<td valign="top">Falling? I think anyone can tilt the frame and suggest a feeling of falling. What makes this special? (Sorry. I do rather like it, but I''m taking issue with titles in this FS.)<br/> <br/>Revisiting this. Title notwithstanding, the tilt does add an interesting dynamic for a guy sitting in a chair in the middle of a crowded street...</td>', 'Falling? I think anyone can tilt the frame and suggest a feeling of falling. What makes this special? (Sorry. I do rather like it, but I''m taking issue with titles in this FS.) Revisiting this. Title notwithstanding, the tilt does add an interesting dynamic for a guy sitting in a chair in the middle of a crowded street...', '2010-08-07 12:48:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121800, 897812, 76335, '<td valign="top">I love this, except... it''s the sun. Looks like you''ve done some selective editing on it. To me it should be the brightest thing in the scene. But the light on the horizon is much brighter.</td>', 'I love this, except... it''s the sun. Looks like you''ve done some selective editing on it. To me it should be the brightest thing in the scene. But the light on the horizon is much brighter.', '2010-08-07 13:29:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121804, 900764, 76335, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. I love the subtle, soft reflection of the sky in the water.</td>', 'Beautiful. I love the subtle, soft reflection of the sky in the water.', '2010-08-07 13:33:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121805, 900439, 76335, '<td valign="top">Very nice, though I wish his face were a bit sharper.</td>', 'Very nice, though I wish his face were a bit sharper.', '2010-08-07 13:33:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121809, 900880, 76335, '<td valign="top">I like this, but since it''s all about form, I wonder if a black and white treatment wouldn''t have been more effective.</td>', 'I like this, but since it''s all about form, I wonder if a black and white treatment wouldn''t have been more effective.', '2010-08-07 13:36:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121816, 900910, 76335, '<td valign="top">Soft and subtle. Watch your highlights.</td>', 'Soft and subtle. Watch your highlights.', '2010-08-07 13:40:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121818, 900267, 76335, '<td valign="top">Wonderful. Your subject is genuine and relaxed. As he''s allegedly the caretaker, I wish for a little more DOF and/or environmental context to see just what he''s taking care of.</td>', 'Wonderful. Your subject is genuine and relaxed. As he''s allegedly the caretaker, I wish for a little more DOF and/or environmental context to see just what he''s taking care of.', '2010-08-07 13:41:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121822, 900916, 76335, '<td valign="top">Maybe better in black and white?</td>', 'Maybe better in black and white?', '2010-08-07 13:43:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121824, 900794, 76335, '<td valign="top">An oddity for sure. I think I like it.</td>', 'An oddity for sure. I think I like it.', '2010-08-07 13:44:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121845, 900443, 76335, '<td valign="top">Bizarre and fascinating. There''s a metaphor here -- and probably an opportunity for analysis of disserational proportion. <br/> <br/>Best of show for me. A ten for you.</td>', 'Bizarre and fascinating. There''s a metaphor here -- and probably an opportunity for analysis of disserational proportion.  Best of show for me. A ten for you.', '2010-08-07 14:11:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121849, 900613, 76335, '<td valign="top">Damn good documentary photography. Those two unoccupied sandals nail it for me.</td>', 'Damn good documentary photography. Those two unoccupied sandals nail it for me.', '2010-08-07 14:13:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121850, 900275, 76335, '<td valign="top">Nature in all its chaos and insanity. This is amazing. Top pick from me.</td>', 'Nature in all its chaos and insanity. This is amazing. Top pick from me.', '2010-08-07 14:13:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121851, 900765, 76335, '<td valign="top">I love the tones here. I almost commented on the yellow spots on the baby''s skin, but deciding to take more than a nanosecond to look at your image, I''ve decided that I like it more because of them. (I know that they''re flowers of course.) <br/> <br/>Not your run-of-the-mill baby portrait. Very good.</td>', 'I love the tones here. I almost commented on the yellow spots on the baby''s skin, but deciding to take more than a nanosecond to look at your image, I''ve decided that I like it more because of them. (I know that they''re flowers of course.)  Not your run-of-the-mill baby portrait. Very good.', '2010-08-07 14:13:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121853, 900766, 76335, '<td valign="top">Pure joy. Nice subtle details all around. Great!</td>', 'Pure joy. Nice subtle details all around. Great!', '2010-08-07 14:23:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121855, 896425, 76335, '<td valign="top">A stunning light show. I love it.</td>', 'A stunning light show. I love it.', '2010-08-07 14:23:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121857, 900106, 76335, '<td valign="top">Painterly. Quite beautiful.</td>', 'Painterly. Quite beautiful.', '2010-08-07 14:24:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121858, 900356, 76335, '<td valign="top">Magically delicious.</td>', 'Magically delicious.', '2010-08-07 14:24:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121859, 899742, 76335, '<td valign="top">Beautifully composed. I like the warm muted colors.</td>', 'Beautifully composed. I like the warm muted colors.', '2010-08-07 14:24:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121860, 898948, 76335, '<td valign="top">Looks like a car ad. Nicely done.</td>', 'Looks like a car ad. Nicely done.', '2010-08-07 14:24:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121861, 900825, 76335, '<td valign="top">An offering to the Basketball God. Great summer fun candid capture.</td>', 'An offering to the Basketball God. Great summer fun candid capture.', '2010-08-07 14:24:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121862, 900980, 76335, '<td valign="top">Very bizarre. Not sure what to think. I do think I like it, however...</td>', 'Very bizarre. Not sure what to think. I do think I like it, however...', '2010-08-07 14:24:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121864, 900850, 76335, '<td valign="top">Beautifully otherworldly.</td>', 'Beautifully otherworldly.', '2010-08-07 14:24:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121865, 900973, 76335, '<td valign="top">The narrow DOF works well on this -- the way the teeth go in and out of focus as the viewer follows them. It has an elliptical sort of rhythm to it.</td>', 'The narrow DOF works well on this -- the way the teeth go in and out of focus as the viewer follows them. It has an elliptical sort of rhythm to it.', '2010-08-07 14:25:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121866, 900299, 76335, '<td valign="top">The otherwise mundane turns intriguing.</td>', 'The otherwise mundane turns intriguing.', '2010-08-07 14:25:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121867, 900215, 76335, '<td valign="top">I''m on the fence here. Is this Topaz or HDR? Normally I hate the look of it, but I''m having a hard time not liking this. Maybe it''s the fact that you retained some black shadow areas, and so the picture has some depth. I like the colors, and I love the scene.</td>', 'I''m on the fence here. Is this Topaz or HDR? Normally I hate the look of it, but I''m having a hard time not liking this. Maybe it''s the fact that you retained some black shadow areas, and so the picture has some depth. I like the colors, and I love the scene.', '2010-08-07 14:25:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121870, 895203, 76335, '<td valign="top">This is incredible. Are those people that appear to be moving toward us? Very ominous. The martian-like foreground textures add to the intrigue.</td>', 'This is incredible. Are those people that appear to be moving toward us? Very ominous. The martian-like foreground textures add to the intrigue.', '2010-08-07 14:25:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121871, 900816, 76335, '<td valign="top">Simply simple. I love it.</td>', 'Simply simple. I love it.', '2010-08-07 14:25:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121873, 900736, 76335, '<td valign="top">A beautiful tapestry.</td>', 'A beautiful tapestry.', '2010-08-07 14:25:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121874, 900727, 76335, '<td valign="top">Fabulous! Usually there''s some jawdropping landscape framing star trails. It''s nice to see this backdrop against the suburban skyline.</td>', 'Fabulous! Usually there''s some jawdropping landscape framing star trails. It''s nice to see this backdrop against the suburban skyline.', '2010-08-07 14:25:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121875, 898274, 76335, '<td valign="top">Holy cow, that''s insane! Such playful violence...</td>', 'Holy cow, that''s insane! Such playful violence...', '2010-08-07 14:25:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121876, 898750, 76335, '<td valign="top">This is screaming for a black and white treatment. Excellent as shown, however.</td>', 'This is screaming for a black and white treatment. Excellent as shown, however.', '2010-08-07 14:26:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121877, 897869, 76335, '<td valign="top">Tres chic.</td>', 'Tres chic.', '2010-08-07 14:26:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121878, 898920, 76335, '<td valign="top">Rich in texture and subtle details. Full of ominous energy. Love it.</td>', 'Rich in texture and subtle details. Full of ominous energy. Love it.', '2010-08-07 14:26:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121879, 898561, 76335, '<td valign="top">Simple and direct. I like that it''s soft and that the contrast isn''t cranked. Makes it more personal.</td>', 'Simple and direct. I like that it''s soft and that the contrast isn''t cranked. Makes it more personal.', '2010-08-07 14:26:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121880, 900671, 76335, '<td valign="top">Both. Or maybe neither. But definitely one or the other. (Or not.) <br/> <br/>Excellent.</td>', 'Both. Or maybe neither. But definitely one or the other. (Or not.)  Excellent.', '2010-08-07 14:26:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121881, 900648, 76335, '<td valign="top">This has a wonderful sort of dark beauty to it. The feeling of decay and death contrast sharply with the lightness of the image. Very effective. Amazing in black and white.</td>', 'This has a wonderful sort of dark beauty to it. The feeling of decay and death contrast sharply with the lightness of the image. Very effective. Amazing in black and white.', '2010-08-07 14:26:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121882, 900754, 76335, '<td valign="top">Cherubesque!</td>', 'Cherubesque!', '2010-08-07 14:26:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121883, 896135, 76335, '<td valign="top">What an ugly beauty! Fantastic rendering of this creature.</td>', 'What an ugly beauty! Fantastic rendering of this creature.', '2010-08-07 14:26:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121884, 900330, 76335, '<td valign="top">Amazing feeling of space and depth here. Excellent.</td>', 'Amazing feeling of space and depth here. Excellent.', '2010-08-07 14:26:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121885, 900497, 76335, '<td valign="top">They look like tentacles. Full of life.</td>', 'They look like tentacles. Full of life.', '2010-08-07 14:26:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121903, 900848, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice silhouette. This has such a peaceful serene feel. Great colortone.</td>', 'Very nice silhouette. This has such a peaceful serene feel. Great colortone.', '2010-08-07 14:52:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121905, 900712, 23484, '<td valign="top">The wheat is contrasted well against the viaduct.</td>', 'The wheat is contrasted well against the viaduct.', '2010-08-07 14:53:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121906, 900621, 23484, '<td valign="top">This kind of processing works so well with very busy cluttered scenes. Nice job.</td>', 'This kind of processing works so well with very busy cluttered scenes. Nice job.', '2010-08-07 14:54:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121907, 900481, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very interesting lights.</td>', 'Very interesting lights.', '2010-08-07 14:55:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121911, 900616, 86218, '<td valign="top">Lovely portrait of cat and love the processing here. Lighting perfect. A bit tight at the top. Those eyes have it</td>', 'Lovely portrait of cat and love the processing here. Lighting perfect. A bit tight at the top. Those eyes have it', '2010-08-07 14:56:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121912, 900789, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very neat structure and nicely composed.</td>', 'Very neat structure and nicely composed.', '2010-08-07 14:56:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121915, 900782, 86218, '<td valign="top">Cute and nice portrait. Unusual comp for this and maybe odd with nose so close to frame on the left. 7</td>', 'Cute and nice portrait. Unusual comp for this and maybe odd with nose so close to frame on the left. 7', '2010-08-07 15:03:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121916, 900927, 86218, '<td valign="top">Nice. Lighting a bit harsh but still a very pleasing shot</td>', 'Nice. Lighting a bit harsh but still a very pleasing shot', '2010-08-07 15:04:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121917, 900871, 86218, '<td valign="top">A bit more depth on this would be nice but still a very nice unusual take on this. I like it.</td>', 'A bit more depth on this would be nice but still a very nice unusual take on this. I like it.', '2010-08-07 15:09:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6121991, 896425, 102278, '<td valign="top">Nice image. Love the light. I have no interest whatsoever whether it is straight out of the camera or not though as that information has nothing to do with a viewers engagement with the final image.  As such i find that part of the title distracting and slightly annoying. Doesn''t make any difference to the score i give though.</td>', 'Nice image. Love the light. I have no interest whatsoever whether it is straight out of the camera or not though as that information has nothing to do with a viewers engagement with the final image.  As such i find that part of the title distracting and slightly annoying. Doesn''t make any difference to the score i give though.', '2010-08-07 16:22:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6122007, 900441, 99263, '<td valign="top">Comment not acknowledged thus removed.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-08-08 05:35:04.</i></td>', 'Comment not acknowledged thus removed.', '2010-08-07 16:52:22.000000', '2010-08-08 06:35:04.000000', 1),
