(6123021, 898825, 110792, '<td valign="top">If anyone is curious about the lighting, I used 24W (equivalent to 100W of light) CFL bulbs mounted on a clamp reflector. Three on the top right, two on the bottom left. These provide really nice soft light. <br/> <br/>Post-processing is simple and the key is something that I do on most on my pictures: I use a duplicate layer with the usual Gaussian blur in soft light layer mode and another layer with a High Pass filter set to around 50%, with an adjustment layer set to saturation. I slightly decrease saturation until I find the right colors.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the great feedback! This was a really fun photo shoot! <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-08-08 12:30:58.</i></td>', 'If anyone is curious about the lighting, I used 24W (equivalent to 100W of light) CFL bulbs mounted on a clamp reflector. Three on the top right, two on the bottom left. These provide really nice soft light.  Post-processing is simple and the key is something that I do on most on my pictures: I use a duplicate layer with the usual Gaussian blur in soft light layer mode and another layer with a High Pass filter set to around 50%, with an adjustment layer set to saturation. I slightly decrease saturation until I find the right colors. Thanks for the great feedback! This was a really fun photo shoot! ', '2010-08-08 12:53:38.000000', '2010-08-08 13:30:58.000000', 0),
